I hope this revision serves our team well. The comments have been written with clarity in mind so that **all colleagues**, regardless of their familiarity with the original Python code, can follow along comfortably.

> 🤝 I would warmly welcome any feedback from the team or our senior colleagues before we move forward with this. If there are any aspects that could be expressed more clearly or aligned better with our existing coding standards, please do not hesitate to share your thoughts.

# Adding an Interactive Tooltip to Your SVG

*I'd like to share this with the team's approach in mind — something clean and maintainable that everyone can comfortably work with. Here are a few approaches, and perhaps we can consider which fits best with how the broader codebase is structured.*

---

## Approach 1: Pure SVG Tooltip (No Dependencies)

This keeps everything self-contained, which may feel more comfortable for the team:

```svg
