## Getting Column Data by Column Label String in wxGrid

The approach that has worked well for our team involves **first finding the column index from the label**, then **retrieving the cell value from that column and row**.

### Step 1: Find Column Index from Label String

```cpp
int FindColumnByLabel(wxGrid* grid, const wxString& labelToFind)
{
    int colCount = grid->GetNumberCols();

    for (int col = 0; col < colCount; col++)
    {
        if (grid->GetColLabelValue(col) == labelToFind)
        {
            return col; // return the matching column index
        }
    }

    return -1; // not found, handle gracefully
}
```

---

### Step 2: Retrieve Cell Value from Specific Row

```cpp
wxString GetCellDataByColumnLabel(wxGrid* grid,
                                   const wxString& columnLabel,
                                   int row)
{
    int col = FindColumnByLabel(grid, columnLabel);

    // It would be wise to check this before proceeding
    if (col == -1)
    {
        // Perhaps log this situation rather than cause disruption
        wxLogWarning("Column label '%s' was not found.",
                      columnLabel);
        return wxEmptyString;
    }

    // Also verify row is within acceptable range
    if (row < 0 || row >= grid->GetNumberRows())
    {
        wxLogWarning("Row index %d is out of range.", row);
        return wxEmptyString;
    }

    return grid->GetCellValue(row, col);
}
```

